KNOWNBUG gcc-only gcc16 libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
std::bind with a call through a deducing-this member, with the headers of
libstdc++ 16, whose code paths differ from gcc 11-15 (tagged libstdcxx16:
runs only where the host gcc is 16 or later, regression/README.md).  With
those headers main was dropped (CONVERSION ERROR at <functional> line 654,
the __enable_if_t default argument evaluated false) until a templated
explicit object parameter was deduced from the object expression
(cpp23_deducing_this_template_object_parameter, header-free).  To check
elsewhere, preprocess with g++-16 -E and run cbmc on the .ii file.
